(5503218, 792924, 41337, '<td valign="top">Crisp clean shot. The lighting and composition are all fine. The diagonal aspect and POV adds appeal but overall there''s nothing here that really grabs you and holds on.</td>', 'Crisp clean shot. The lighting and composition are all fine. The diagonal aspect and POV adds appeal but overall there''s nothing here that really grabs you and holds on.', '2009-05-28 03:27:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(5503233, 793073, 41337, '<td valign="top">The problem with copying someone else''s shot is you need to meet or exceed the original otherwise you''re doomed to the inevitable comparision. Unfortunately, since this one doesn''t have the originality/creativity associated with it your technicals needed to be better just to break even, which is why it''s better to just try out something new. It''s that whole risk/reward thing, which you''re avoiding here. <br/> <br/>That said, I understand people try to recreate a photo just to learn but bare in mind that as a voter I must consider more than just the technicals, which is all you have focused on here so you lose a lot in the voting from me.</td>', 'The problem with copying someone else''s shot is you need to meet or exceed the original otherwise you''re doomed to the inevitable comparision. Unfortunately, since this one doesn''t have the originality/creativity associated with it your technicals needed to be better just to break even, which is why it''s better to just try out something new. It''s that whole risk/reward thing, which you''re avoiding here.  That said, I understand people try to recreate a photo just to learn but bare in mind that as a voter I must consider more than just the technicals, which is all you have focused on here so you lose a lot in the voting from me.', '2009-05-28 03:46:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5503234, 793955, 41337, '<td valign="top">Not bad but lighting and the arrangement is a little too basic, IMO.</td>', 'Not bad but lighting and the arrangement is a little too basic, IMO.', '2009-05-28 03:47:34.000000', NULL, 1),
